{"parentUuid":"632b2e73-3824-4f04-961d-c7ee7ca42d3f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2602275c-a7ed-40db-b819-ed697f71606e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nI went through the conversation in order. The user first reported that some photo uploads were failing; I looked at the logs and the configuration, made a change, reloaded the service and tried a large test photo, which went through. The user then asked for faster uploads; I changed how the upload request does its work and ran the photo tests, which passed. Each request is covered in the numbered sections below, with the files it touched and where the work stood when the context ran out.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Fix photo uploads that fail with 413 for files over about 1 MB.\n   - Make uploads faster by moving thumbnail generation out of the request.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - nginx request body limits, Celery queues and task routing, Django file storage.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - deploy/nginx.conf: server block of the app.\n   - recipes/tasks.py: new make_thumbnails task.\n   - recipes/photos.py: PhotoUploadView no longer resizes inline.\n   - spoonful/celery.py: task routes.\n   - docker-compose.yml: new worker-thumbs service.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Uploads over 1 MB failed with 413 Request Entity Too Large because deploy/nginx.conf had no body size setting, so nginx used its 1m default and rejected the body before Django saw it. Fix: client_max_body_size 20m in the server block, matching the 20 MB limit that Django's upload validator already enforces, so both layers agree and Django returns its friendly error for anything larger.\n\n5. Key decisions:\n   - Thumbnails are generated by the thumbs queue: a Celery task on a dedicated `thumbs` queue with its own worker (concurrency 2) creates the three sizes after the upload, instead of resizing inside the request. The upload returns at once with thumbnail_status \"pending\". A dedicated queue keeps a burst of uploads from delaying the email and search-index tasks on the default queue.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Users can't upload photos bigger than about 1 MB, they get a 413. Can you look into it?\"\n   - \"Great. While you're at it, uploads are slow because we resize in the request. Can we move that out?\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - None beyond the two requests above.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The photo tests passed (11). The upload endpoint returns in about 90 ms and thumbnails appear shortly after."},"uuid":"93680194-3de6-49e9-b809-931ea1729364","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:11:00.521Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":3,"turnIndex":3},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"slug":"s29-quiet-harbor","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/user/spoonful","sessionId":"163c66d4-caf0-4d51-a4da-50889cc630cb","version":"2.1.300","gitBranch":"feat/async-thumbs"}
